    "model": "conversational-exchange",
    "note_for_team": "Angrez Stage 2 'Everyday Talk' v2. Changes from v1: (1) directions sub-stage removed (Google Maps made it redundant); (2) negotiation is now a real back-and-forth — counter-offers, follow-up questions/statements, and free add-on requests ('throw in some coriander'), built as CHAINED single-exchange role_play_turns so it feels multi-turn while staying inside the MVP single-exchange limit (true multi-turn is Phase 2); (3) two expressive sub-stages added — feelings/family check-in (2.6) and reviews/opinions (2.7) — a difficulty step up from transactions to saying how you feel and what you think. Two teach types: 'ask' (learner speaks first) and 'exchange' (prompt -> 3 natural responses). Speech is primary; 'fallback' is the no-mic path. All six MVP puzzle types appear. l1 = natural Devanagari, warm, never shaming. accept[] is forgiving.",
    "design_rules": {
      "responses_per_prompt": 3,
      "negotiation": "Chain single-exchange turns to simulate haggling: ask price -> shopkeeper counters -> learner counters/follows up -> learner asks for a free add-on -> close. Accept any natural counter; never fail on word order if intent is clear.",
      "expressive": "Feelings and opinions have no single 'right' answer — accept[] lists are wide and open_ended:true; the win is speaking a natural opinion, not matching a target.",
      "indian_english": "Bargaining, free add-ons (dhania/chillies), autos, rupees, 'make it less', 'last price', 'na' — keep it real to Tier 2/3 daily life.",
      "numbers": "Accept spoken number or digits in prices/fares."
    },
    "audio_convention": {
      "english": "audio/en/<key>.mp3 — AI-TTS, native Indian-English + RP",
      "hindi": "audio/hi/<key>.mp3 — Hindi prompts, AI-TTS",
      "regenerable": true
    },
    "image_convention": "img/s2/<name>.webp — simple, clear, compressed.",
